This code sets up a Rails API application that allows users to upload a video file and specify a frame number to extract. The application uses `ffmpeg` to process the video and extract the specified frame as a PNG image. The extracted image is then sent back to the user, or an error message is returned if the frame cannot be found. 

To run the application, ensure you have `ffmpeg` installed and execute the command `bin/rails server --binding 0.0.0.0 --port 5000`.
